Oh, one thing to consider: the EotA actually makes a temporary portal
to your stash, and some monsters will follow you through.  Still
great, since then you're fighting them in *your* territory instead of
theirs. But consider this and prepare for it; put your stash on the
first level of Sokoban, since the EotA will send you to the lowest
level of the branch you choose that you've been through, and Sokoban
has a safe and consistent lowest level.  Then burn Elbereth in a few
places, including under a locked chest with your stuff in it.

I also like keeping an icebox with a cockatrice corpse in it,
in case I Demogorgon follows me up.  If you put an icebox there when
you first find one, then you can branchport straight to it when you
find a rubber chicken and you don't have to worry about it rotting
away while you run to the box.

