As opposed to wasting scrolls.  If you luck out and get +7, great. But
don't worry about it otherwise.  The damage from ranged weapons comes
from advancing your skill to the point where you're throwing 3 of them
in one turn, not from that last point of enchantment.

I also have a paranoid habit of keeping my gear enchanted to the point
where I can safely enchant it one more time, since I'd rather have
a slightly worse AC/damage than risk accidentally vaporizing an
irreplaceable artifact through carelessness.  Generally by the time
I have enough scrolls to enchant everything to that point, ascension
is almost guaranteed anyway; it's the early game I have trouble with.
Daggers are worth the risk, though; there are always more daggers to
be found.

